# Trivy ignore file. Each entry needs a justification; re-review on expiry.
# Auto-loaded for filesystem scans from the repo root; image scans receive
# it explicitly via `trivyignores:` in .github/workflows/security.yml.

# CVE-2026-40345 (deepmerge-ts 7.1.5, stack exhaustion on recursive merges).
# Dev-only transitive dep: prisma CLI (@prisma/config) used at build time to
# generate the client. Never shipped: devDependencies are pruned from runtime
# images and it is absent from all production bundles. The only fixed release
# is breaking-major 8.x, which prisma 6 pins against (exact 7.1.5); revisit on
# the prisma 7 upgrade. Unreachable at runtime.
# exp: 2027-03-01
CVE-2026-40345

# AVD-KSV-0110 (workloads in the default namespace): the chart deliberately
# leaves namespace unset so `helm install -n <env>` scopes releases per
# environment; hardcoding a namespace would break multi-env installs.
# Namespace governance belongs to cluster admission policy.
AVD-KSV-0110

# AVD-KSV-0125 (images from untrusted registries): the registry is an
# install-time value (global.imageRegistry, default ghcr.io); it cannot be
# resolved statically by design. Allowed registries belong to cluster
# admission policy.
AVD-KSV-0125

# AVD-DS-0026 (no HEALTHCHECK in Dockerfiles): liveness/readiness is defined
# at the orchestration layer (probes in this Helm chart, healthchecks in
# docker-compose for infra, `make smoke` for dev). A Dockerfile-level check
# would duplicate that and cannot be parameterized across the four services
# sharing one Dockerfile without new build args.
AVD-DS-0026
